Technical Specification and Economic Balancing: Crafting Recipe Architecture, Progression Tiering, and JEI Integration for NeoForge 1.21Game Balancing and Vanilla Material EconomyThe integration of high-throughput vehicle mechanics into Minecraft introduces severe systemic balance disruptions. A functional spaceship compiled via Breadth-First Search (BFS) capable of mobilizing up to $10{,}000\text{ blocks}$ with transactional cross-dimensional teleportation, localized Voronoi energy shielding, and high-yield offensive laser systems alters survival gameplay loops. Left unregulated, unmetered access to dynamic 6-axis flight, structural invulnerability, and rapid block vaporization eliminates the challenges of terrain traversal, environmental hazard mitigation, and dimensional resource logistics. Establishing an unyielding economic progression using vanilla materials ensures that capital ship construction remains a deliberate, mid-to-endgame pursuit rather than an early-game exploit.Progression Tiering Philosophy and Dimensional GatingTechnological capability in the mod is partitioned across a strict four-tier hierarchy. Progression moves linearly through dimensional gates, anchoring technical capabilities to distinct vanilla survival milestones.In Tier 1, designated as Terrestrial Navigation and Structural Framework, operations are confined entirely to Overworld resources such as iron, copper, redstone, slimeballs, and quartz. This tier permits players to frame hulls, establish aesthetic bridges, and construct kinetic utility tools without granting active flight capabilities.Tier 2 represents Sub-Orbital Utility and Local Defense, introducing baseline automation, localized hexagonal Voronoi barrier projection, and initial energy storage capped at $1{,}000{,}000\text{ FE}$. Progression into Tier 2 requires basic Nether colonization to acquire Nether Quartz, Blaze Rods, and Obsidian, complemented by crystalline Overworld elements including Amethyst Shards and Diamonds. At this level, laser technology is restricted to industrial mining drills operating at $25\text{ FE/t}$, designed explicitly to excavate minerals without inflicting entity damage.Tier 3 introduces Naval-Grade Offensive Weaponry, transitioning laser systems into continuous thermal beams consuming $50\text{ FE/t}$ and kinetic burst cannons drawing $250\text{ FE/shot}$. The resource requirements shift into deep Nether excavation for Netherite Scrap and Crying Obsidian, alongside Deep Dark exploration for Echo Shards. These demands prevent players from deploying long-range block vaporizers or hull-melting beams prior to mastering high-threat vanilla environments.Tier 4 represents Capital Entity Kernels and Dimensional Warping, centered entirely on the Spaceship Controller (peaceman_alpha:spaceship_control). This block functions as the computational brain executing the 6-axis BFS assembly algorithm and cross-dimensional transit calculations. Constructing this kernel demands materials from the outer End dimension and the defeat of the Wither boss, including Nether Stars, Lodestones, End Crystals, and Eyes of Ender.The economic cost of gating functional ship assembly behind the Nether and the End addresses both game pacing and computational load. Compiling a $10{,}000\text{ block}$ structure into an active entity imposes heavy strain on world generation streaming, chunk meshing, and server thread ticks. Requiring a Lodestone mandates netherite synthesis, tethering vessel navigation to physical coordinate anchors. Gating trans-dimensional warping behind Nether Stars and End Crystals guarantees that players conquer baseline dimensions before executing transactional spatial shifts.Material Progression MatrixThe distribution of vanilla materials across the technological tiers aligns functional capabilities with survival resource rarities:Component IdentifierFunctional DesignationProgression TierDimensional RequirementPrimary Vanilla IngredientsEconomic and Functional Purposepeaceman_alpha:example_blockHull Plating / ChassisTier 1OverworldIron Ingot, Copper Ingot, Smooth StoneMass-produced structural framework (yields 16 per craft) designed to mitigate BFS volume costs.peaceman_alpha:spaceship_helmSpaceship Helm ConsoleTier 1OverworldSmooth Stone, Compass, Redstone Dust, Glass Pane, Iron IngotCockpit console for orientation. Low material cost allows aesthetic vessel design prior to core commissioning.peaceman_alpha:backflip_toolBackflip ToolTier 1OverworldIron Sword, Piston, Slimeball, Redstone DustKinetic utility sword providing localized entity launching and emergency pilot repositioning.peaceman_alpha:mining_laserMining Laser TurretTier 2Nether (Entry)Diamond, Nether Quartz, Copper Block, Dispenser, Redstone BlockIndustrial drill turret ($25\text{ FE/t}$). Requires quartz focus lenses and diamond cutting heads; deals zero entity damage.peaceman_alpha:spaceship_reactorSpaceship Reactor ($1\text{M FE}$)Tier 2NetherBlaze Rod, Nether Quartz, Iron Block, Redstone Block, DiamondHigh-density thermal containment cell. Blaze rods function as thermal stabilizers and quartz provides dielectric insulation.peaceman_alpha:spaceship_shieldShield GeneratorTier 2NetherAmethyst Shard, Obsidian, Diamond Block, Eye of EnderProjects 3D Voronoi partitions. Amethyst provides harmonic frequency refraction, while obsidian dampens blast impulses.peaceman_alpha:pulse_laserPulse Laser CannonTier 3Deep Nether / Ancient CityNetherite Scrap, Echo Shard, Crying Obsidian, Redstone Block, ObserverBurst turret ($250\text{ FE/shot}$). Echo shards focus acoustic-kinetic force into plasma; observers govern pulse timing.peaceman_alpha:heavy_beamHeavy Laser BeamTier 3Netherite / Nether FortressNetherite Ingot, Magma Cream, Blaze Rod, Nether Quartz, Diamond BlockContinuous thermal beam ($50\text{ FE/t}$). Netherite frames prevent thermal melting under sustained electrical discharge.peaceman_alpha:spaceship_controlSpaceship ControllerTier 4The End / Wither BossNether Star, Lodestone, End Crystal, Eye of Ender, Netherite BlockComputational entity kernel and dimensional warp core. High cost prevents early-game deployment of capital hulls.Grid Layouts and Thematic JustificationsThematic consistency demands that crafting recipes reflect the mechanical operation of each ship component through logical material arrangements:Component IdentifierStation TypeGrid Row 1 (Left to Right)Grid Row 2 (Left to Right)Grid Row 3 (Left to Right)Output Yieldpeaceman_alpha:example_blockCrafting TableCopper Ingot, Iron Ingot, Copper IngotIron Ingot, Smooth Stone, Iron IngotCopper Ingot, Iron Ingot, Copper Ingot16peaceman_alpha:spaceship_helmCrafting TableIron Ingot, Glass Pane, Iron IngotRedstone Dust, Compass, Redstone DustSmooth Stone, Smooth Stone, Smooth Stone1peaceman_alpha:backflip_toolCrafting TableEmpty, Slimeball, Iron SwordEmpty, Piston, SlimeballRedstone Dust, Empty, Empty1peaceman_alpha:spaceship_reactorCrafting TableIron Block, Quartz Block, Iron BlockBlaze Rod, Redstone Block, Blaze RodDiamond, Iron Block, Diamond1peaceman_alpha:spaceship_shieldCrafting TableObsidian, Amethyst Shard, ObsidianAmethyst Shard, Eye of Ender, Amethyst ShardObsidian, Diamond Block, Obsidian1peaceman_alpha:mining_laserCrafting TableCopper Block, Nether Quartz, Copper BlockNether Quartz, Diamond, Nether QuartzIron Block, Dispenser, Redstone Block1peaceman_alpha:spaceship_controlCrafting TableNetherite Block, End Crystal, Netherite BlockEye of Ender, Nether Star, Eye of EnderLodestone, Netherite Block, Lodestone1peaceman_alpha:heavy_beamSmithing TableTemplate: Netherite UpgradeBase: Mining LaserAddition: Netherite Ingot1peaceman_alpha:pulse_laserSmithing TableTemplate: Netherite UpgradeBase: Mining LaserAddition: Echo Shard1The structural logic of these recipes reflects their mechanical function in the game world. Hull Plating (peaceman_alpha:example_block) yields sixteen blocks per synthesis because large BFS hulls require substantial volumes of building materials. Copper acts as an outer conductive sheath against electrical discharge, iron ingots provide structural rigidity, and smooth stone forms the compressed aggregate core.The Spaceship Helm (peaceman_alpha:spaceship_helm) arranges an iron casing around a central navigation compass, flanked by redstone bus wiring and an upper glass pane that represents a cockpit display console.The Backflip Tool (peaceman_alpha:backflip_tool) uses an iron sword as a directional blade, mounted over an angled mechanical piston and cushioned by elastic slimeballs to convert stored redstone impulse energy into physical entity propulsion.For energy and defense systems, the Spaceship Reactor (peaceman_alpha:spaceship_reactor) balances thermal generation and containment. Blaze rods regulate internal heating, a central redstone block provides the electrical reservoir, quartz blocks provide dielectric resistance, and dense iron and diamond platings absorb high-energy flux.The Shield Generator (peaceman_alpha:spaceship_shield) surrounds an Eye of Ender with four Amethyst Shards, utilizing crystalline lattice resonance to project hexagonal Voronoi geometries, while an obsidian perimeter and a diamond block base absorb impact forces.The Mining Laser (peaceman_alpha:mining_laser) uses a dispenser payload base, quartz focusing optics, and a central diamond cutter housed inside heat-radiating copper blocks.The Spaceship Controller (peaceman_alpha:spaceship_control) represents the pinnacle of technology in the mod. It places a Nether Star at the center to serve as the autonomous computational engine. Dual Lodestones anchor positional vectors in three-dimensional space, an End Crystal channels dimensional rift energy for warp jumps, and Netherite blocks contain the gravitational forces generated during entity conversion.Crafting Station Mechanics: Crafting Table versus Smithing Table UpgradesA critical design choice is whether combat laser turrets (heavy_beam, pulse_laser) should be crafted directly in a standard 3x3 Crafting Table or upgraded from the industrial mining_laser using a Smithing Table.Employing the Smithing Table via SmithingTransformRecipe provides clear mechanical and economic advantages. The primary architectural benefit is the preservation of Data Components. Upgrading an item in a Smithing Table automatically transfers custom data components—such as energy charge, internal temperature history, kill tallies, or optical lens configurations—from the base mining_laser to the upgraded combat turret. By contrast, standard crafting recipes overwrite component attachments unless specialized, dynamically bound recipe serializers are introduced.From a balance perspective, routing military laser systems through the Smithing Table prevents players from skipping early industrial steps. The player must first assemble the utility-focused mining_laser before modifying it into an offensive naval weapon.Furthermore, integrating the minecraft:netherite_upgrade_smithing_template introduces an ongoing resource sink. Players must spend seven diamonds and one netherrack block to duplicate the template for every turret upgrade, preventing rapid naval stockpiling.This upgrade path also improves gameplay pacing: transitioning an industrial mining tool into a high-powered beam weapon through netherite reinforcement feels like a natural technological evolution.Automated DataGen Implementation in NeoForge 1.21Modern data generation establishes compile-time validation for recipe JSON declarations, ensuring that advancements, ingredients, and recipe definitions remain synchronized. NeoForge 1.21 refactors several recipe generation systems, updating RecipeProvider, RecipeOutput, and advancement trigger registries.RecipeProvider Architecture in NeoForge 1.21In NeoForge 1.21, a custom recipe provider must extend net.minecraft.data.recipes.RecipeProvider. The provider constructor receives a PackOutput path instance and a CompletableFuture<HolderLookup.Provider> asynchronous registry lookup. Recipe declarations are defined by overriding the protected void buildRecipes(RecipeOutput output) method.The RecipeOutput interface manages generated data serialization. It takes the recipe name, recipe instance, and generated advancement criteria, outputting JSON definitions directly to data/<modid>/recipe/ and data/<modid>/advancement/recipes/. NeoForge extends RecipeOutput with #withConditions, allowing runtime data conditions to be attached directly to recipe outputs during generation.Recipe Builders and Idiomatic APIsShapedRecipeBuilder: Instantiated using ShapedRecipeBuilder.shaped(RecipeCategory, ItemLike, int). Patterns are defined through .pattern(String), where each string row must have a consistent character width. Symbols are mapped via .define(Character, ItemLike) or .define(Character, Ingredient). Unlocking criteria are added via .unlockedBy(String, Criterion<?>), and recipes are finalized by calling .save(RecipeOutput, ResourceLocation).SmithingTransformRecipeBuilder: Instantiated via SmithingTransformRecipeBuilder.smithing(Ingredient template, Ingredient base, Ingredient addition, RecipeCategory category, Item result). Unlocking criteria are attached using .unlocks(String, Criterion<?>), and the recipe is saved via .save(RecipeOutput, ResourceLocation).Advancement Criteria (unlockedBy): Data generation requires every recipe builder to specify at least one unlock criterion; omitting this triggers an IllegalStateException during compile-time tasks. The helper method RecipeProvider.has(ItemLike) generates an InventoryChangeTrigger.TriggerInstance. To ensure recipes appear logically in the player's recipe book, triggers should track key signature materials (for example, unlocking the spaceship reactor when Items.BLAZE_ROD enters the inventory).Production Implementation: ModRecipeProvider.javaJavapackage com.peaceman.alpha.datagen;

import com.peaceman.alpha.registry.ModBlocks;
import com.peaceman.alpha.registry.ModItems;
import net.minecraft.core.HolderLookup;
import net.minecraft.data.PackOutput;
import net.minecraft.data.recipes.RecipeCategory;
import net.minecraft.data.recipes.RecipeOutput;
import net.minecraft.data.recipes.RecipeProvider;
import net.minecraft.data.recipes.ShapedRecipeBuilder;
import net.minecraft.data.recipes.SmithingTransformRecipeBuilder;
import net.minecraft.resources.ResourceLocation;
import net.minecraft.world.item.Items;
import net.minecraft.world.item.crafting.Ingredient;

import java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;

public class ModRecipeProvider extends RecipeProvider {

    public ModRecipeProvider(PackOutput output, CompletableFuture<HolderLookup.Provider> lookupProvider) {
        super(output, lookupProvider);
    }

    @Override
    protected void buildRecipes(RecipeOutput output) {
        // =====================================================================
        // TIER 1: LOW-TIER / NAVIGATION & HULL
        // =====================================================================

        // Hull Plating / Chassis (Yield: 16)
        ShapedRecipeBuilder.shaped(RecipeCategory.BUILDING_BLOCKS, ModBlocks.EXAMPLE_BLOCK.get(), 16)
                .pattern("CIC")
                .pattern("ISI")
                .pattern("CIC")
                .define('C', Items.COPPER_INGOT)
                .define('I', Items.IRON_INGOT)
                .define('S', Items.SMOOTH_STONE)
                .unlockedBy("has_iron_ingot", has(Items.IRON_INGOT))
                .unlockedBy("has_copper_ingot", has(Items.COPPER_INGOT))
                .save(output, ResourceLocation.fromNamespaceAndPath("peaceman_alpha", "example_block_crafting"));

        // Spaceship Helm
        ShapedRecipeBuilder.shaped(RecipeCategory.MISC, ModBlocks.SPACESHIP_HELM.get())
                .pattern("IGI")
                .pattern("RCR")
                .pattern("SSS")
                .define('I', Items.IRON_INGOT)
                .define('G', Items.GLASS_PANE)
                .define('R', Items.REDSTONE)
                .define('C', Items.COMPASS)
                .define('S', Items.SMOOTH_STONE)
                .unlockedBy("has_compass", has(Items.COMPASS))
                .save(output, ResourceLocation.fromNamespaceAndPath("peaceman_alpha", "spaceship_helm_crafting"));

        // Backflip Tool
        ShapedRecipeBuilder.shaped(RecipeCategory.COMBAT, ModItems.BACKFLIP_TOOL.get())
                .pattern(" SB")
                .pattern(" PS")
                .pattern("R  ")
                .define('B', Items.IRON_SWORD)
                .define('S', Items.SLIME_BALL)
                .define('P', Items.PISTON)
                .define('R', Items.REDSTONE)
                .unlockedBy("has_slime_ball", has(Items.SLIME_BALL))
                .save(output, ResourceLocation.fromNamespaceAndPath("peaceman_alpha", "backflip_tool_crafting"));

        // =====================================================================
        // TIER 2: MID-TIER / MINING & LOCAL DEFENSE
        // =====================================================================

        // Spaceship Reactor (1,000,000 FE Storage)
        ShapedRecipeBuilder.shaped(RecipeCategory.MISC, ModBlocks.SPACESHIP_REACTOR.get())
                .pattern("IQI")
                .pattern("BRB")
                .pattern("DID")
                .define('I', Items.IRON_BLOCK)
                .define('Q', Items.QUARTZ_BLOCK)
                .define('B', Items.BLAZE_ROD)
                .define('R', Items.REDSTONE_BLOCK)
                .define('D', Items.DIAMOND)
                .unlockedBy("has_blaze_rod", has(Items.BLAZE_ROD))
                .save(output, ResourceLocation.fromNamespaceAndPath("peaceman_alpha", "spaceship_reactor_crafting"));

        // Shield Generator
        ShapedRecipeBuilder.shaped(RecipeCategory.MISC, ModBlocks.SPACESHIP_SHIELD.get())
                .pattern("OAO")
                .pattern("AEA")
                .pattern("ODO")
                .define('O', Items.OBSIDIAN)
                .define('A', Items.AMETHYST_SHARD)
                .define('E', Items.ENDER_EYE)
                .define('D', Items.DIAMOND_BLOCK)
                .unlockedBy("has_amethyst_shard", has(Items.AMETHYST_SHARD))
                .unlockedBy("has_ender_eye", has(Items.ENDER_EYE))
                .save(output, ResourceLocation.fromNamespaceAndPath("peaceman_alpha", "spaceship_shield_crafting"));

        // Mining Laser Turret
        ShapedRecipeBuilder.shaped(RecipeCategory.MISC, ModBlocks.MINING_LASER.get())
                .pattern("CQC")
                .pattern("QDQ")
                .pattern("IBR")
                .define('C', Items.COPPER_BLOCK)
                .define('Q', Items.QUARTZ)
                .define('D', Items.DIAMOND)
                .define('I', Items.IRON_BLOCK)
                .define('B', Items.DISPENSER)
                .define('R', Items.REDSTONE_BLOCK)
                .unlockedBy("has_diamond", has(Items.DIAMOND))
                .save(output, ResourceLocation.fromNamespaceAndPath("peaceman_alpha", "mining_laser_crafting"));

        // =====================================================================
        // TIER 3: HIGH-TIER / COMBAT WEAPONS (SMITHING TRANSFORMATION)
        // =====================================================================

        // Heavy Laser Beam (Upgraded from Mining Laser + Netherite Ingot)
        SmithingTransformRecipeBuilder.smithing(
                Ingredient.of(Items.NETHERITE_UPGRADE_SMITHING_TEMPLATE),
                Ingredient.of(ModBlocks.MINING_LASER.get()),
                Ingredient.of(Items.NETHERITE_INGOT),
                RecipeCategory.COMBAT,
                ModBlocks.HEAVY_BEAM.get().asItem()
        )
        .unlocks("has_netherite_ingot", has(Items.NETHERITE_INGOT))
        .save(output, ResourceLocation.fromNamespaceAndPath("peaceman_alpha", "heavy_beam_smithing"));

        // Pulse Laser Cannon (Upgraded from Mining Laser + Echo Shard)
        SmithingTransformRecipeBuilder.smithing(
                Ingredient.of(Items.NETHERITE_UPGRADE_SMITHING_TEMPLATE),
                Ingredient.of(ModBlocks.MINING_LASER.get()),
                Ingredient.of(Items.ECHO_SHARD),
                RecipeCategory.COMBAT,
                ModBlocks.PULSE_LASER.get().asItem()
        )
        .unlocks("has_echo_shard", has(Items.ECHO_SHARD))
        .save(output, ResourceLocation.fromNamespaceAndPath("peaceman_alpha", "pulse_laser_smithing"));

        // =====================================================================
        // TIER 4: ENDGAME-TIER / SHIP CORE & WARP DRIVE
        // =====================================================================

        // Spaceship Controller (BFS Assembly Kernel & Warp Core)
        ShapedRecipeBuilder.shaped(RecipeCategory.MISC, ModBlocks.SPACESHIP_CONTROL.get())
                .pattern("NEN")
                .pattern("YSY")
                .pattern("LNL")
                .define('N', Items.NETHERITE_BLOCK)
                .define('E', Items.END_CRYSTAL)
                .define('Y', Items.ENDER_EYE)
                .define('S', Items.NETHER_STAR)
                .define('L', Items.LODESTONE)
                .unlockedBy("has_nether_star", has(Items.NETHER_STAR))
                .unlockedBy("has_lodestone", has(Items.LODESTONE))
                .save(output, ResourceLocation.fromNamespaceAndPath("peaceman_alpha", "spaceship_control_crafting"));
    }
}
Pipeline Registration: DataGenerators.javaThe recipe provider must be bound to the mod event bus within GatherDataEvent. Because recipe and advancement generation are server-side assets, registration must be guarded by event.includeServer() to prevent execution during client-only data runs.Javapackage com.peaceman.alpha.datagen;

import net.minecraft.core.HolderLookup;
import net.minecraft.data.DataGenerator;
import net.minecraft.data.PackOutput;
import net.neoforged.bus.api.SubscribeEvent;
import net.neoforged.fml.common.EventBusSubscriber;
import net.neoforged.neoforge.data.event.GatherDataEvent;

import java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;

@EventBusSubscriber(modid = "peaceman_alpha", bus = EventBusSubscriber.Bus.MOD)
public class DataGenerators {

    @SubscribeEvent
    public static void gatherData(GatherDataEvent event) {
        DataGenerator generator = event.getGenerator();
        PackOutput packOutput = generator.getPackOutput();
        CompletableFuture<HolderLookup.Provider> lookupProvider = event.getLookupProvider();

        // Server-side Data Providers (Recipes, Advancements, Loot Tables, Tags)
        if (event.includeServer()) {
            generator.addProvider(
                true, 
                new ModRecipeProvider(packOutput, lookupProvider)
            );
        }

        // Client-side Data Providers (BlockStates, ItemModels, Language)
        if (event.includeClient()) {
            // Existing client providers execute here...
        }
    }
}
Just Enough Items (JEI) and Recipe Viewer CompatibilityVanilla Recipe Discovery and Gradle ConfigurationIn NeoForge 1.21, Just Enough Items indexes recipes directly from the logical server's synchronized RecipeManager and RecipePropertySet data streams. Standard recipes generated via ModRecipeProvider—including minecraft:crafting_shaped, minecraft:crafting_shapeless, and minecraft:smithing_transform—are indexed, categorized, and made searchable automatically without requiring custom mod-side Java code.To compile against the JEI API and test recipes in local development environments, add Jared's Maven repository and the corresponding NeoForge dependencies to build.gradle:Groovyrepositories {
    maven {
        name = "BlameJared Maven"
        url = "https://maven.blamejared.com/"
    }
}

dependencies {
    // Compile against the JEI API without packaging it inside the mod jar
    compileOnly("mezz.jei:jei-1.21.1-neoforge-api:19.21.1.304")

    // Run JEI in local development client runs
    runtimeOnly("mezz.jei:jei-1.21.1-neoforge:19.21.1.304")
}
