Data Components in Minecraft 1.21 RecipesMinecraft 1.21 replaces legacy CompoundTag NBT systems with typed Data Components managed via DataComponentType<?> and DataComponentMap. This update changes recipe serialization, ingredient matching, and recipe viewer integration.Standard vanilla Ingredient classes check only base item definitions and tags, ignoring attached components. To require an item with specific component states—such as a battery cell with pre-charged energy or a pre-calibrated laser focus lens—recipes must use NeoForge's custom DataComponentIngredient. In recipe providers, this is constructed using DataComponentIngredient.of(boolean strict, ItemStack stack).Setting strict to false verifies that an item possesses the specified target components while allowing other non-conflicting components to remain present. Setting strict to true requires an exact match across all data components. In serialized JSON files, this generates the neoforge:components ingredient type:JSON{
  "type": "neoforge:components",
  "items": "peaceman_alpha:energy_cell",
  "strict": false,
  "components": {
    "peaceman_alpha:energy_stored": 250000
  }
}
Standard recipe builders output default, unmodified item states by default. To generate recipes that output items with pre-configured data components, such as a fully charged reactor or a pre-linked helm, the builder must accept an ItemStack containing a DataComponentPatch. The serialized JSON stores these in the "components" mapping within the "result" object:JSON"result": {
  "count": 1,
  "id": "peaceman_alpha:spaceship_reactor",
  "components": {
    "peaceman_alpha:energy_stored": 1000000
  }
}
JEI inspects the DataComponentMap of output ItemStack instances, rendering dynamic tooltips, durability bars, energy capacity indicators, and custom component-based styling. For DataComponentIngredient inputs, JEI cycles through the accepted item stacks and displays their component information, allowing players to verify required charge states or lens tunings before crafting.ConclusionsBalancing high-tier vehicle systems requires coordinating resource gating, crafting station mechanics, and data-driven infrastructure. Requiring Nether and End resources for structural controllers, Voronoi energy shields, and naval laser turrets prevents players from bypassing survival milestones, ensuring that capital ship construction integrates smoothly into late-game survival progression.The DataGen pipeline automates recipe creation and maintenance. Extending RecipeProvider within NeoForge 1.21 establishes compile-time safety and generates the required advancement triggers automatically, eliminating manual JSON authoring.Using SmithingTransformRecipeBuilder to upgrade mining lasers into combat turrets reinforces industrial progression while preserving attached Data Components across transformations.Finally, building on vanilla recipe systems allows JEI to index all shaped, shapeless, and smithing recipes automatically. A lightweight IModPlugin then handles custom UI layouts, click areas, and modern 1.21 Data Component inputs. This unified architecture provides a balanced, technically sound foundation for spaceship combat and progression in NeoForge 1.21.
